ec2:

tags :   Tags are key-value pairs used to identify, organize, and manage AWS resources.
ami:  AMI (Amazon Machine Image) is a template used to launch EC2 instances.
        types of AMI's
        1) community ami's
        2) marketplace AMI's
        3) My AMi's

instance type and family:
    --> instance family is a category of EC2 instances designed for a specific type of workload.
    --> instance type  is the specific size/configuration within a family.
key-pairs: A key pair is a set of two keys (public key and private key) used to securely connect to an EC2 instance via SSH.
        1) public key  (which resides inside the home user directory for ubuntu it is -----> /home/ubuntu/.ssh/autherizedd_file)
        2) private key (pem file)
Networking settings:
        1) network : Network refers to the VPC where your EC2 instance will be created.
        2) subnet: Subnet is a smaller network inside a VPC.
        3) security Group: Security Group acts as a virtual firewall for EC2 instances.
EBS: configuration:
        BS is block storage used as a disk for EC2 instances.

        👉 It is used for:
            OS (root volume)
            Application data
            Logs / databases

additional details:
        userdata
        termination protection
        change shutdown protection
        change stop protection


